Thanks James! 

I'm almost ashamed to admit it, but I didn't have the cord plugged in.

On that note, the separate = FALSE function in the write.amelia command, for example:

write.amelia(obj=bgdata.mi, separate = FALSE, file.stem = "bgdata.mi", format = "dta")

Will also not work unless you have the new version of R. I ended up using the append manually in Stata yesterday, but had I been using the newest version of R, I could have avoided that! Thanks again. 

-Kyle

